      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I think this is a great idea, though, there would probably need to be a data change so things can be solved better. For example: There should be a flag for *which* moderation actions were done by who, or if it was done by a \"moderator\" and not \"owner\".\n\nThis way, the moderators can not undo or change moderation actions that the main user did. Obviously you should be careful who you pick as your moderators, but this would still prevent abuse or reduce accidents.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
